# Divider Component Features

## Core Features

### Orientation
- Horizontal divider (default)
  - Renders as semantic `<hr>` element
  - Full-width horizontal line
  - Default orientation when not specified

- Vertical divider
  - Renders as `<div>` with `role="separator"`
  - Full-height vertical line
  - Used in flex/grid layouts to separate content side-by-side

## Props

### orientation
- Type: `'horizontal' | 'vertical'`
- Default: `'horizontal'`
- Description: Controls the direction of the divider line

### className
- Type: `string`
- Optional
- Description: Additional CSS classes for custom styling

### ariaLabel
- Type: `string`
- Optional
- Description: Accessible label for screen readers to provide context

### testId
- Type: `string`
- Optional
- Description: Data attribute for testing frameworks

## Styling

### BEM Classes
- Base: `.aceui-divider`
- Horizontal modifier: `.aceui-divider--horizontal`
- Vertical modifier: `.aceui-divider--vertical`

### Design Tokens
- Border color: `--aceui-color-border-default`
- Border width: `--aceui-border-width-small`

## Accessibility

### Horizontal Divider
- Uses semantic `<hr>` element
- Native separator role
- Optional `aria-label` for context

### Vertical Divider
- Uses `role="separator"`
- `aria-orientation="vertical"` attribute
- Optional `aria-label` for context

## Usage Patterns

### Between Sections
- Separate content blocks vertically
- Visual hierarchy in layouts

### In Navigation
- Separate menu items with vertical dividers
- Create visual groupings

### In Card Layouts
- Divide card header, body, and footer
- Separate related content sections

### In Flex/Grid Layouts
- Vertical dividers in multi-column layouts
- Side-by-side content separation
